13	  Implement batched dense Cholesky factorization.
14	
15	  Input is `A`, a `batch x n x n` CUDA tensor in `torch.float32`. Every matrix
16	  is symmetric positive definite up to FP32 roundoff. Return a lower-triangular
17	  FP32 tensor `L` with positive diagonal such that `A = L @ L.T`.
18	
19	  The checker validates shape, dtype, device, finiteness, lower-triangular
20	  structure, positive diagonal, and the reconstruction residual against the
21	  original FP32 input. Correctness is property-based rather than elementwise
22	  comparison with one library implementation.
23	
24	  Inputs cover dense covariance-like matrices, planted spectra, diagonal
25	  matrices, damped low-rank matrices, scaled rows and columns, and
26	  tridiagonal SPD matrices. The `cond` field is a deterministic dynamic-range
27	  control; it is not an exact requested condition number for every case.
28	
29	  The benchmark grid emphasizes batched factorization: from thousands of small
30	  matrices through a single 32768 x 32768 matrix. The low-batch entries from
31	  n=32 through n=1024 each contain 2^22 FP32 input elements, so matrix scaling
32	  is compared at a consistent 16 MiB input footprint. Paired high-batch entries
33	  at n=512, 1024, 2048, and 4096 separately exercise throughput and batch
34	  parallelism. Among passing submissions, ranking is by the geometric mean of
35	  runtime across all benchmark entries.
